──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
SURFACE PARITY — what was ported from the web source (no scope narrowing)
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
• Composition : Sparkles header + title (Subhead) + description (Caption) + disc-bulleted preview list of the
                archived-feature labels + trailing "No thanks" (ghost) / "Restore selection" (primary) actions —
                every region of AIRestorePanel.tsx.
• previewLabels: faithfully ported (AIRestorePreview.labels) — walks the archived entries IN ORDER, drops the
                `false` ones, resolves a known feature id to t(`ai.settings.feature.<id>.label`, AI_FEATURES[id].name)
                and renders an unknown id verbatim (raw id) so the listing is never blank.
• AI_FEATURES : the frozen 57-feature id→name table + isKnownAiFeature ported verbatim into AIFeatureCatalog.
• role=alert  : web `role="alert" aria-live="polite"` → a contained accessibility element whose label announces
                title + description + the resolved feature names (AIRestoreAccessibility.summary seam).
• onConfirm / onDecline : forwarded through the P1/S8 state-holder seam (AIRestoreSource.confirm/decline); the view
                issues no HTTP. ADR-015 §I7 "restore is never silent" preserved (explicit confirm vs decline).
• States      : loading (skeleton chrome) / empty (nothing enabled → friendly ContentUnavailableView, never blank) /
                error (QueryError peer + retry) / data, PLUS the orthogonal connection axis live/stale/offline
                (freshness chip + banner + one-shot stale auto-refresh) — the P4 leaf contract.
• i18n        : 100% via the P1/S10 facade (AIRestoreStrings, table "AIRestorePanel"); zero English literals in
                Swift beyond the web-default fallbacks (the established AcDcStatsPanel/0096 pattern).
• Telemetry   : P1/S11 `view.opened` emitted once with surface slug "AIRestorePanel".
• a11y        : VoiceOver labels on every interactive element (decline, restore, refresh, retry), Dynamic Type via
                Font.TS roles, Reduce-Motion-aware fade-in + skeleton shimmer.

